      "writtenOn": "2023-02-15T15:10:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is there a reason we can\u0027t simply always make this true? If the caller enabled connection migration on path degradation, then presumably they want to migrate stuck requests regardless of whether the requests get stuck before the handshake or after it.\n\nIIRC this was not supported by the initial migration code but was only added later (and resulted in a major improvement in the effectiveness of connection migration). Perhaps that\u0027s why it\u0027s a flag. But is there any reason for it to continue to be a flag now?\n\nDo you know if anyone intentionally sets it to false?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 48,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 48,
        "endChar": 81
      },
      "revId": "fb4c1af99c74e3e83920e28c39553041c2aba779",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
